<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea to absorb 500 bln won from banks.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea to absorb 500 bln won from banks.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea plans to absorb 500 billion won from the banking system on Friday through three-day repurchase agreements with commercial banks, an official at the central bank said.</p>
<p>He said there was about two trillion won in surplus cash liquidity in the money market.</p>
<p>He gave no further details.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
